/* *   EventHandlers.incl - what happens when the user does something * *   Starting template from Imagery LogicBank Studio for FutureBasic: created once, then *   yours.  Regeneration never overwrites it (delete it to get a fresh copy). *   <project>.main registers these three functions with FutureBasic's event loop: *       on appevent fn DoAppEvent      the application (launch, quit, ...) *       on menu     fn DoMenu          a menu choice *       on dialog   fn DoDialog        anything in a window: clicks, table selections, ... * *   Developer notes *   - The generated behaviour lives in other files; each handler below passes the event *     on, in order, until one says "mine" (returns YES).  Put your own handling before a *     call (to change what happens) or after it (to add to it). *   - DoDialog's order:  the window frame (App Shell.incl: navigation, theme menu)  -> *     the pages (App Pages.incl: lists and forms)  ->  your Log In button  ->  the ALS *     runtime (ALS App.incl, used by apps that talk to an API Logic Server). *   - ev, tag and wnd: the event (_btnClick, _tableViewSelectionDidChange, ...), the tag of *     the control it came from (Model Tags.incl names every generated one), the window. */// fblint: AppPagesDoDialog is in App Pages.incl, which the generator writes beside this file// generated: AppPagesDoDialogvoid local fn DoAppEvent( ev as long )fn ALSDoAppEvent( ev )                     // e.g. quit when the last window closesend fnvoid local fn DoMenu( menuID as long, itemID as long )fn ALSDoMenu( menuID, itemID )             // the Records menu: New, Save, Delete, Refreshend fn// the header's Log In button - connect it to your sign-in (an API Logic Server login, ...)void local fn DoLoginalert 1, NSAlertStyleInformational, @"Log In", @"Connect this button to your sign-in in EventHandlers.incl (DoLogin).", @[@"OK"], NOend fnvoid local fn DoDialog( ev as long, tag as long, wnd as long )if ( fn ShellDoDialog( ev, tag, wnd ) ) then exit fn          // navigation and the theme menuif ( fn AppPagesDoDialog( ev, tag, wnd ) ) then exit fn       // a list's selection fills its formif ( ev == _btnClick && tag == _shellLoginButton )fn DoLoginexit fnend iffn ALSDoDialog( ev, tag, wnd )                                 // the ALS runtime's window, when it is usedend fn